CANON CORRECTIONS APPLIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. XERXES IS A MAN, AND ALSO THREE PLACES. Xerxes is a half-elf half-human
   individual; the city, the planet and the system are all named after him
   (author, 2026-08-30). The place the mod currently scripts is ruled by
   Vaelorin Sylvaerath, "The Tide-Crowned" (see events/eotg_xerxes_events.txt),
   and its faith is eotg_faith_firstlight — Vaelorin rules the city named for
   Xerxes, he is not Xerxes.
   A hero-veneration faith is therefore viable, but the old draft's supporting
   details are not yet canon: that Xerxes is dead, and that he led a resistance
   against the Elrossi Crusade, appear nowhere except that draft. See BACKLOG F.

2. ORRIN IS NOT IMPRISONED. Per the SETTING LORE ERRATA (2026-08-29), the Void
   was Orrin's prison but no longer holds him; he is in the material plane. The
   Void still exerts an influence and that influence is UNEXPLAINED. The old
   draft's "imprisoned deity" framing for Orrin's Conquest is superseded. In
   text, attributing Void phenomena to Orrin is a BELIEF characters hold, never
   narrated fact.

3. THE GOBLINS HAVE THEIR OWN RELIGION. Two things are true at once (author,
   2026-08-30): canon puts Bohemut, Son of Yu (Balance, Knowledge, Equilibrium)
   at the centre of merchant and scholarly worship, AND the goblins — merchant-
   focused as they are — follow a religion of their own rather than his. Both
   are now implemented and they are deliberately not the same religion:
   eotg_religion_commerce (the Profitable Path, Bohemite, Divine Order) and
   eotg_religion_plutocracy (the Plutocracy, goblin, Pragmatic Codes). They
   trade side by side inside the Gob-Ogre Trade League and argue about whether
   the sacred act is the exchange or the accumulation.

4. THE RATFOLK FAITH IS ANCESTOR VENERATION, AND IT IS CALLED DEEP WARREN
   (author, 2026-08-30). Note the near-collision: eotg_religion_deep_warren is
   the ratfolk ancestor faith, while eotg_religion_ancestor_veneration is the
   *Broken Daimyo* lineage faith of Titanworld refugees. Two ancestor religions,
   two different peoples, similar-sounding keys — check which one you mean.
   Both sit in eotg_rf_ancestral.

5. DEITIES THE OLD DRAFT MISSED. Canon includes FERROS (Lawful Evil; Conquest,
   Tyranny, Domination — Orrin pantheon) and THE HIEROPHANT (Divine Judge, of
   unclear origin and allegiance). Neither appeared in the 27.

6. ORRO BELONGS TO THE ORRIN PANTHEON (author, 2026-08-30). SETTING LORE lists
   him under CURRENT DIVINE ENTITIES ("Death God, ACTIVE, OMINOUS") but omitted
   him from the COSMOLOGY & DEITIES roster, leaving his alignment ambiguous.
   Resolved: he is an Orrin-pantheon deity, alongside Ferros, Sanguis, Kyros,
   Ravos, Vexis and Ikarath. Applied throughout — Orro is now named in the
   EvilGodNames of the order-aligned faiths and among the Void cult's own.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REAL CK3 1.19 SCHEMA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Paths (1.19 layout — Tiger 1.17 still expects the old 1.16 paths, see GAPS):
  common/religion/religion_types/          religions + their faiths
  common/religion/religion_family_types/   families
  common/religion/doctrine_types/          (vanilla; we define none)
  common/religion/holy_site_types/         holy sites

A religion takes: family, graphical_faith, piety_icon_group,
doctrine_background_icon, pagan_roots, doctrine (single-pick only),
traits = { virtues sins }, reserved_male_names / reserved_female_names,
custom_faith_icons, localization = { }, holy_order_names, holy_order_maa,
and finally faiths = { }. Doctrines cannot appear after the faiths block.

A faith takes: color, icon, religious_head, holy_site (any number),
doctrine, reserved names, localization, holy_order_names.

TENETS ARE FAITH-LEVEL, NOT RELIGION-LEVEL. doctrine_core_tenets has
number_of_picks = 3, and the engine forbids multi-pick doctrine groups at
religion level (there is no override system that would work). Every faith
therefore carries exactly three `doctrine = tenet_*` lines.

There are no per-faith "modifiers" blocks. Mechanical effects come from the
tenets and doctrines you pick; anything beyond that needs a real system
(scripted modifiers, on_actions, events) built separately.

Family-level `hostility_doctrine` sets cross-family hostility. Only four exist:
abrahamic_, pagan_, eastern_ and sinitic_hostility_doctrine.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RELIGION FAMILIES (4)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
eotg_rf_divine_order    hostility: abrahamic    Yu and his sons.
  Elross, Commerce (Bohemut), Coldiron (Frozt), Firstlight.

eotg_rf_titan_worship   hostility: pagan        Looks past the sons to the Titans.
  Void Reverence. Reserved for future Carrigore and Orrin cults.

eotg_rf_ancestral       hostility: pagan        The dead, the lineage, the work.
  Stampede, Ancestor Veneration, Forge Tradition, Deep Warren.

eotg_rf_pragmatic       hostility: pagan        Non-theistic codes and craft.
  Survivalism, Secular Codes, Plutocracy.
  The odd one out is the Plutocracy, which is materialist rather than civic —
  it grants the Hoard exactly the reverence the other two refuse any god. It
  belongs here on the shared premise (nothing above you is owed obedience for
  its own sake) rather than on temperament, and the three would argue.

NOTE ON COMMERCE: it previously sat in eotg_rf_titan_worship behind a "TODO:
define proper mercantile faith family" comment, which contradicted its own
localization — Bohemut is explicitly a Son of Yu. Moved to Divine Order.

UNRESOLVED TENSION — VOID REVERENCE: the religion description is Malvrick-
centric, and Malvrick is a Son of Yu, which argues for Divine Order. The faith
beneath it (eotg_faith_void_cult) venerates the breach itself and argues about
what answers from the empty prison, which is Titan-facing. It stays in
eotg_rf_titan_worship on the strength of the faith rather than the religion.
Worth revisiting if a second, more orthodox Malvrick faith is ever added.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPLEMENTED — 12 RELIGIONS, 13 FAITHS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All shipped in common/religion/religion_types/eotg_religions.txt with full
adjective / adherent / adherent_plural / desc localization in
localization/english/eotg_religions_l_english.yml, and god-name localization
blocks backed by localization/english/eotg_religion_gods_l_english.yml.

1. eotg_religion_elross — family eotg_rf_divine_order
   Elross, Son of Yu: light as obligation, justice owed, righteousness enforced.
   Backbone of the Second Elrossi Imperium. Acting openly since 850 AG.
   virtues = { just brave zealous }   sins = { arbitrary craven cynical }
   FAITH eotg_faith_elross_canonical — Orthodox Elrossi, governed from Elyria.
     tenets: unrelenting_faith, armed_pilgrimages, legalism

2. eotg_religion_commerce — family eotg_rf_divine_order
   Bohemut, Son of Yu: balance as accounting. Merchants and scholars read the
   same scripture and reliably take different lessons from it.
   virtues = { diligent honest temperate }   sins = { lazy deceitful greedy }
   FAITH eotg_faith_commerce — Creed-Sworn; a contract honoured is a prayer
     completed. tenets: pursuit_of_knowledge, ritual_hospitality, legalism

2b. eotg_religion_plutocracy — family eotg_rf_pragmatic
   The goblin faith. Not Bohemut's balance and not a rival reading of it — a
   different religion, which holds that the sacred act is accumulation rather
   than exchange, and that a sum which stops growing has died. Recognises no
   god because it considers one unnecessary: the Hoard is observable and
   answers in proportion to effort invested.
   virtues = { greedy diligent ambitious }   sins = { generous lazy content }
   FAITH eotg_faith_goblin_plutocracy — as kept in the counting-vaults of the
     Gob-Ogre Trade League. Worth is public and continuously measured, which
     makes it brutally meritocratic. Its assessors tax unbelievers as a
     devotional act. tenets: tax_nonbelievers, pursuit_of_power, adaptive

3. eotg_religion_coldiron — family eotg_rf_divine_order
   Frozt: cold and loss as curriculum. Warrior-monks of the Caliphate who treat
   comfort as a form of dishonesty.
   virtues = { temperate patient brave }   sins = { gluttonous impatient craven }
   FAITH eotg_faith_coldiron — the Covenant; endurance rather than victory.
     tenets: exaltation_of_pain, monasticism, asceticism

4. eotg_religion_firstlight — family eotg_rf_divine_order
   The elven light-faith, older than the Elrossi canon and unwilling to be
   absorbed into it. Light is tended, not obeyed.
   virtues = { patient compassionate humble }   sins = { impatient callous arrogant }
   FAITH eotg_faith_firstlight — dawn observances, unbroken lamps, long memory.
     tenets: sun_worship, ritual_celebrations, pursuit_of_knowledge

5. eotg_religion_void_reverence — family eotg_rf_titan_worship
   Malvrick, the son nobody wants: darkness, secrets, and the Void that was
   built as Orrin's prison, does not hold him, and has not gone quiet.
   virtues = { eccentric ambitious callous }   sins = { content humble compassionate }
   FAITH eotg_faith_void_cult — venerates the breach itself. Capital offence
     across most of settled space. tenets: esotericism, sacred_destruction,
     human_sacrifice

6. eotg_religion_stampede — family eotg_rf_ancestral
   The centaur faith: the dead run ahead, the living are obliged not to break
   stride. Clan oaths are sworn to the Run, so breaking one is theft from the dead.
   virtues = { honest brave gregarious }   sins = { deceitful craven lazy }
   FAITH eotg_faith_stampede — the Khanate's codified Run, hardened by the War
     of Broken Hooves. tenets: ancestor_worship, ritual_hospitality,
     communal_identity

7. eotg_religion_ancestor_veneration — family eotg_rf_ancestral
   Broken Daimyo lineage faith. Asks nothing of the pantheons and everything of
   lineage. The Grip killed enough ancestors to make the practice urgent.
   virtues = { humble diligent honest }   sins = { arrogant lazy deceitful }
   FAITH eotg_faith_ancestor_veneration — Name-Keepers; the rolls are kept,
     recited, and consulted before anything irreversible.
     tenets: ancestor_worship, filial_piety, communal_identity

8. eotg_religion_forge_tradition — family eotg_rf_ancestral
   Stone endures. Foundation over flourish; haste is a species of cowardice.
   Absorbs the old draft's "Thalvoria's Foundation" (mountains, stability,
   building) — the mountain halls and the ogre foundries share this faith.
   virtues = { patient diligent stubborn }   sins = { impatient lazy fickle }
   FAITH eotg_faith_forge_tradition — a life measured by what it left standing.
     tenets: mountain_worship, megaliths, communal_identity

9. eotg_religion_deep_warren — family eotg_rf_ancestral
   The ratfolk ancestor faith. Each deep gallery was cut by a named generation
   and the names are kept, so going further down is going further back. Depth is
   holy, and abandoning a gallery is desertion rather than retreat.
   virtues = { patient paranoid diligent }   sins = { trusting arrogant lazy }
   FAITH eotg_faith_deep_warren — a Deepkeeper can recite which forebear cut
     which gallery, and consults them before digging: the dead are asked for
     precedent rather than blessing.
     tenets: ancestor_worship, cthonic_redoubts, pastoral_isolation

10. eotg_religion_survivalism — family eotg_rf_pragmatic
    The Grip proved the universe will not catch you; machinery did. The sacred
    act is maintenance; a god who needs prayer is less use than a working pump.
    virtues = { diligent temperate patient }   sins = { lazy gluttonous wrathful }
    FAITH eotg_faith_industrial_survivalism — Creedwrights of the salvage
      sectors and Helix remnants. Scripture is a maintenance log.
      tenets: communal_identity, pursuit_of_knowledge, adaptive

11. eotg_religion_secular_codes — family eotg_rf_pragmatic
    Not a denial that the gods exist — since 850 AG that is hard to hold in
    public — but a refusal to let them hold office. Power that cannot be
    audited is owed no obedience.
    virtues = { just honest diligent }   sins = { arbitrary deceitful lazy }
    FAITH eotg_faith_secular_contract — the mercenary companies' code. Terms are
      met, clients are not betrayed mid-engagement.
      tenets: warmonger, legalism, adaptive
    FAITH eotg_faith_civic_secular — New Cauldron's founding conviction, kept
      seven centuries. The franchise itself is the sacred thing.
      tenets: legalism, communal_identity, pursuit_of_knowledge

