--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BACKLOG — PRIORITY ORDER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. eotg_religion_carrigore (family eotg_rf_titan_worship). The rising threat all
   major powers fear. Two faiths: eotg_faith_cult_of_cosmos (organised, ambitious,
   Samulo the Stardrinker as demigod exemplar) and eotg_faith_feral_star
   (uncoordinated frontier shamans practising crude star drinking). Needs the
   Star Drinking system to mean anything mechanically; until then it is two
   faiths with tenets and no unique behaviour. Coordinate with the existing Void
   Corruption system — Carrigore corruption must not simply mirror it.

B. eotg_religion_gorgath (family eotg_rf_divine_order — Gorgath is a Yu-aligned
   elder deity). The Aphionian Consortium's secret society. Obvious tenets:
   esotericism, pursuit_of_knowledge, astrology.

C. eotg_religion_orrin (family eotg_rf_titan_worship). Orrin Warparty. Must be
   written under the errata: Orrin is loose in the material plane, and nobody
   in-world can say what still speaks from the empty Void.

D. Secondary Yu deities as FAITHS rather than religions — Serephios, Solena,
   Mystara, Core, Zephyrion, Lunara. Each is one deity with a following, not a
   separate cosmology; folding them in as faiths under existing religions is
   cheaper and reads better than eleven near-empty religions.

E. Orrin pantheon secondaries — Ferros, Sanguis, Kyros, Ravos, Vexis, Ikarath
   and Orro. Same reasoning: faiths under eotg_religion_orrin.

F. A Xerxes hero-veneration faith. Viable now that Xerxes is established as a
   person (canon #1), but two things must be settled first, because the only
   source for either is the discarded draft:
     - Is Xerxes dead? A veneration cult reads very differently if he is not.
     - Did he lead a resistance against the Elrossi Crusade? The draft built the
       whole faith on this and nothing else in the project corroborates it.
   If both hold, it slots in as a faith rather than a religion — most likely
   under eotg_religion_firstlight, since the city named for him already keeps
   that faith, which would make the cult a schism among the Firstlit rather
   than a new cosmology. That is a more interesting position than the draft's
   free-floating resistance religion, and it costs one faith instead of eleven.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN GAPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOLY SITES — none defined, for any faith. Blocked on the map pass: baronies have
no province IDs yet, so there is nothing to anchor a holy site to. Faiths
currently run with zero holy sites, which leaves the faith screen's five slots
empty and gives Great Holy Wars nothing to target. Unblock with the map pass,
then add 3–5 per major faith.

TIGER IS BLIND HERE — ck3-tiger 1.17 looks for religions in
common/religion/religions/ (the 1.16 layout) and CK3 1.19 uses
common/religion/religion_types/. Tiger therefore never parses these files and
reports every faith reference elsewhere in the mod as "not defined in
common/religion/religions/". Those ~54 errors are false positives, and the
corollary matters more: Tiger provides NO validation of religion content. Every
doctrine, tenet and trait name in these files has to be checked against vanilla
by hand.

GRAPHICAL FAITH — all families still borrow vanilla gfx (christian_gfx,
pagan_gfx) and vanilla doctrine background icons. Tracked in docs/art_needed.txt.

HOLY ORDERS — no holy_order_names or holy_order_maa on any religion, so holy
orders fall back to "holy_order_default" with randomly generated coats of arms.
Cheap to fix once the sci-fi men-at-arms set is settled.

RESERVED NAMES — no reserved_male_names / reserved_female_names on any religion.
Low priority.

